{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5178) that requires implementing srd005-wc requirements R2.5-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 in the existing `cmd/wc` utility. Specifically:\n   - **R2.5**: `-L` flag prints the length of the longest line (tab-expanded to next multiple of 8 columns). Independent of other flags, combinable with any.\n   - **R2.6**: Combined flags print counts in fixed order: lines (`-l`), words (`-w`), chars (`-m`) or bytes (`-c`), max-line-length (`-L`) — regardless of user flag order.\n   - **R3.1**: Multi-file output must right-align counts in columns wide enough for the largest count across all files (dynamic column-width).\n   - **R3.2**: Total line uses label \"total\" (not filename), counts are arithmetic sums of all files.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/wc/main.go` and `cmd/wc/wc_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require passing `go test ./cmd/wc/... -count=1` and `go vet ./cmd/wc/...`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `gwc`\n   - `LC_ALL=C` locale for deterministic comparison\n   - Tab expansion for `-L`: each tab advances to next multiple of 8 columns\n   - Fixed output column order independent of flag order on command line\n   - Column-width alignment computed from file size totals (GNU wc behavior)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - DiffTest struct: `{Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, ...}`\n   - Multi-file tests will need file arguments (not just stdin)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd005-wc.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements R2.5, R2.6, R3.1, R3.2\n     - R2.5: `-L` prints longest line length measured in display columns (tab-expanded)\n     - R2.6: Output order is fixed: lines, words, chars/bytes, max-line-length\n     - R3.1: Right-align counts in columns wide enough for largest count across all files\n     - R3.2: Total line label is \"total\", counts are arithmetic sums\n     - Non-goals: No East Asian wide-character display-width handling for -L\n\n   - **cmd/wc/main.go** (existing, 410 lines)\n     - Already has `options` struct with `printMax bool` field for `-L`\n     - Already has `counts` struct with `maxLine int64` field\n     - `countReader` tracks `lineLen` and updates `c.maxLine` at EOF\n     - `processChunk` handles tab expansion via `handleTab`: `*lineLen = (*lineLen/8 + 1) * 8`\n     - `handleNewline` updates `c.maxLine` when `*lineLen > c.maxLine`\n     - `collectFields` outputs in order: lines, words, chars, bytes, maxLine (matches R2.6)\n     - `computeWidth` estimates column width from file sizes (GNU wc approach)\n     - `printResults` handles total line with \"total\" label\n     - `shouldShowTotal` supports auto/always/only/never modes\n     - `parseArgs`/`parseLongFlag`/`parseShortFlags` handle `-L` and `--max-line-length`\n     - Key observation: **R2.5, R2.6, R3.1, R3.2 logic appears already implemented in code**\n\n   - **cmd/wc/wc_test.go** (existing, 176 lines)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gwc\")`\n     - `defaultEnv = []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}`\n     - 25 test cases covering: default flags, individual flags (-l, -w, -c, -m), flag combinations (-lw, -lwc, -lm, -wm, -lwm), empty input, binary input\n     - **Missing test coverage**: No `-L` tests, no multi-file tests, no total line tests, no combined flags with `-L`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed existing code to determine what's already implemented vs. what needs to be added\n   - Found that the core logic for R2.5 (maxLine with tab expansion), R2.6 (fixed output order), R3.1 (column alignment from computeWidth), and R3.2 (total line with \"total\" label) appears to already exist in cmd/wc/main.go from a prior task\n   - The main gap is **test coverage**: no differential tests exist for -L flag, multi-file scenarios, or total line behavior\n   - Multi-file tests will need to create temporary files using WorkDir in DiffTest structs\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive task description message containing: role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description with requirements R1-R4, design decisions D1-D3, acceptance criteria AC1-AC4, shared_protocols, package_contracts, and constraints.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools...\" - instructing me to produce a summary instead of continuing with tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify the existing `-L` implementation is correct for R2.5 (appears implemented)\n   - Verify output column ordering for R2.6 (appears implemented) \n   - Verify multi-file column alignment for R3.1 (appears implemented)\n   - Verify total line for R3.2 (appears implemented)\n   - Add differential test cases to `cmd/wc/wc_test.go` for:\n     - `-L` flag alone and combined with other flags (R2.5)\n     - Combined flag output ordering including `-L` (R2.6)\n     - Multi-file scenarios with column alignment (R3.1)\n     - Total line with multiple files (R3.2)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/wc/...` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/wc/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n   - Must NOT run any git commands (orchestrator handles git)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, wc_test.go) and was about to plan and implement the changes. The analysis showed that the core logic for R2.5-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 already exists in main.go 