{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SoYLub58wCHcmLMxNU6TLJ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found all the information you need. Here's my complete report:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5178/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 46-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Key fields for multi-file testing:**\n- **`Args`**: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries (where file names are specified)\n- **`WorkDir`**: When set, both binaries execute in this directory. When empty, a temp directory is created via `t.TempDir()`\n- **`ExpectedFiles`**: A map of relative file paths to expected byte contents for post-execution validation\n\n## Example of Multi-File Differential Test\n\nFound in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5178/cmd/cat/cat_test.go` (lines 45-58):\n\n```go\nfunc TestDiffFiles(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gcat\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary gcat not found\")\n\t}\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"file1.txt\", \"aaa\\n\")\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"file2.txt\", \"bbb\\n\")\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t{Name: \"multi_file\", Args: []string{\"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"}, WorkDir: dir},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\nThis example demonstrates the multi-file testing pattern:\n1. Creates a temporary directory\n2. Writes fixture files to that directory using a helper function\n3. Defines DiffTest with file names in `Args` and the directory in `WorkDir`\n4. The testutils framework runs both the Go and reference binaries in that `WorkDir` with those arguments, allowing them to access the created files"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3473b47-a5a0-4e0d-947b-e76c77cbd5fa","uuid":"add5fe11-4ed4-47e5-8f1e-47d7250b1dce","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:09:14.654Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5178, I need to:\n\n1. Read the DiffTest struct definition in pkg/testutils/ to see all available fields (especially WorkDir, SetupFunc, or anything for creating temp files)\n2. Find an example in any cmd/*/wc_test.go or cmd/*/*_test.go file that uses file arguments (not just stdin) in DiffTests — i.e., tests that pass filenames as Args and set up temp files\n\nReport the full DiffTest struct definition and any example of multi-file differential tests.","agentId":"a09e16da3363fa2c3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found all the information you need. Here's my complete report:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Definition\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5178/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 46-55):\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n```\n\n**Key fields for multi-file testing:**\n- **`Args`**: Command-line arguments passed to both binaries (where file names are specified)\n- **`WorkDir`**: When set, both binaries execute in this directory. When empty, a temp directory is created via `t.TempDir()`\n- **`ExpectedFiles`**: A map of relative file paths to expected byte contents for post-execution validation\n\n## Example of Multi-File Differential Test\n\nFound in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5